##### SUMMARY
<!--- Explain the problem briefly -->
When gathering facts about DHCP option sets in AWS EC2 VPC the module will fail if an option set has had no tags applied to it. i.e. The default option set will cause this module to bomb out with a traceback.

Note: A default DHCP Option set appears to have tags applied to it when viewing it in the AWS console because it lists:
Key = "Name"
Value = ""
But in reality it has no tags applied to it.

